Easy Lunch Ideas for Busy Period Days

A busy college, school, or work schedule can make it tempting to skip lunch, especially when you are dealing with period discomfort. However, having a simple lunch can help you maintain your energy and keep your day organised.

Rice, dal, and vegetables are an easy combination. Dal provides protein and can contribute iron, rice provides carbohydrates, and vegetables add fibre and other nutrients.

A chickpea wrap can be prepared quickly. Fill a chapati with cooked chickpeas, cucumber, tomatoes, carrots, and greens. Add yoghurt dressing or chutney for extra flavour.

Lemon rice with peanuts and a protein-rich side can also work well. You can add vegetables or serve it with curd and a lentil-based dish.

Chapati with dal and vegetable curry is another practical lunch-box option. Preparing extra portions at dinner can save time the next day.

If you eat eggs, an egg-and-vegetable sandwich can be made quickly. Use whole-grain bread and add tomato, cucumber, lettuce, or other vegetables.

Salads can be made more filling by adding chickpeas, beans, tofu, paneer, eggs, or chicken. A salad does not have to mean eating only raw vegetables.

Try to include different vegetables and fruits throughout the week. Variety can make your meals more enjoyable while helping you obtain a range of nutrients.

If you experience cravings during your period, you can still enjoy your favourite foods. A balanced diet does not require you to completely avoid treats.

Hydration is important too. Carry a water bottle to work or college and drink throughout the day.

It is also worth keeping your period-care products in your bag. A small pouch with spare sanitary pads can be useful if your period starts unexpectedly or your flow is heavier than usual.

Choose a sanitary pad that feels comfortable and matches your flow. Having a product you trust can make it easier to concentrate on your work, studies, or travel.

